its capacity when its cost is negative and nothing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"otherwise. Capacities may be of an unsigned type, up to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int.max","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Computed by the network simplex with block-search pivots and strongly feasible trees.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Which optimum is returned when several exist is unspecified, but the same input always","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gives the same result. ","type":"text"},{"code":"supply","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is called once per vertex in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order, then, for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each edge in position order, ","type":"text"},{"code":"capacity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and then ","type":"text"},{"code":"cost","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", before any work.","type":"text"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every capacity is at least zero; capacities, supplies and costs fit in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"text":"; Σ capacity × |cost| fits in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Cost"},{"text":" (checked before solving, since it bounds the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"total cost); 4(n + 1)(the greatest |cost| of a non-loop edge + 1) fits in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"text":" (the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"solver’s artificial cost, with room for its potentials and reduced costs); the positive","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"supplies sum within ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Capacity"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Precondition"}],"kind":"content"}],"